BNSC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19987, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PhtkiXBzfcxuRPqL1XFxHR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20287, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PhtkiXBzfcxuRPqL1XFxHR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20287, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PhtkiXBzfcxuRPqL1XFxHR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25536, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NGgyybQrFdkJjmtMKu7Cmo", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, it failed health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left versions mixed across regions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished successfully. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollout, and check why a release that was unhealthy in staging went to production."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56136, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NGgyybQrFdkJjmtMKu7Cmo", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56136, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NGgyybQrFdkJjmtMKu7Cmo", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58426, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Bn5rCf4U3pqGQ2n9AM9uDq", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58726, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Bn5rCf4U3pqGQ2n9AM9uDq", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58726, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Bn5rCf4U3pqGQ2n9AM9uDq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64028, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The only newer release, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed in staging.\n- My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the regions on different versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n- I retried the same rollback and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I created INC-0001 for checkout-api at SEV2, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current healthy state.\n- The create request timed out, but the incident list shows it was created, so I didn't retry. That means there's only one incident and one page.\n- Suggested follow-ups, also listed in the incident:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n  - Find out why a release that failed in staging was deployed to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DDBwHAfPiQLagbdUBaxEaM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ND7NZqejLLeU8w5E1KZicB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014SqxWhh4itdK2YyLfyt3Pt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XwJNpUKqYSG7BeS1gtQkkb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through: only us-east moved to v2.3.0. I'll retry once, since rolling back to the same known-healthy version is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NqFQEMKvzYtv2R9geHNfLo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016PDi1uJqxuWRnb1ph6BNSC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PhtkiXBzfcxuRPqL1XFxHR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NGgyybQrFdkJjmtMKu7Cmo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, it failed health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left versions mixed across regions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished successfully. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollout, and check why a release that was unhealthy in staging went to production."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not exist. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Bn5rCf4U3pqGQ2n9AM9uDq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The only newer release, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed in staging.\n- My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the regions on different versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n- I retried the same rollback and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I created INC-0001 for checkout-api at SEV2, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current healthy state.\n- The create request timed out, but the incident list shows it was created, so I didn't retry. That means there's only one incident and one page.\n- Suggested follow-ups, also listed in the incident:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n  - Find out why a release that failed in staging was deployed to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}